{
  "summary": "User Tom Becker (Finance, user_id 4) asked us to release a quarantined email he believes holds copier scans. Quarantine shows Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-08 08:46 UTC, reason MALWARE, not releasable. The sender is an external domain, not an internal copier, and this matches the common fake-scanner malware lure. Not released, per KB-007/KB-008. The user has been told to report and ignore similar mail and to have scans re-sent from the copier directly. Separately: his account is currently LOCKED with 5 failed sign-ins. He didn't mention this, so please review sign-in logs for possible credential attacks. Security team review of Q-1005 is needed. No other users were checked. Q-1004 (a spam invoice from harborview-supplies) is also in his quarantine but he hasn't asked for it.",
  "reason": "Requested message is marked malware; only security can review. Account lockout also needs review."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the email, but I can't release it. Our mail filter flagged the zip file as malware. It also came from an outside address (docs-share.example), not from our office copier, and fake 'scanned document' emails like this are a common way attackers spread harmful files. I've sent it to our security team to review. In the meantime, please scan your documents again and send them from the copier straight to your mailbox. If you get a similar email in your inbox, don't open the attachment: use the Report Phishing button in Outlook, then delete it. One more thing: your account is currently locked after several failed sign-in attempts. If that wasn't you, let us know. Someone from the help desk will follow up.",
  "internal_note": "The requested message is Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject 'Scanned document 0931.zip', received 2026-10-08. It's marked malware and not releasable, so I didn't release it (KB-007/KB-008). The sender is external, which makes this a likely fake-scanner lure. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation 1). Separately, the account is LOCKED with 5 failed logins, which the user didn't mention. I didn't unlock it because he didn't ask and the cause hasn't been checked. Recommend reviewing sign-in logs. Q-1004 (a spam invoice from harborview-supplies) is also in quarantine. He didn't request it, so I didn't touch it.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
